                <pb facs="0331" n="259" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg259"/>

                <head>No. 45.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. West to Earl Granville.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 28, 1882</date>.
                        (Received April 10.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to inclose to your lordship herewith, copy of a letter from one
                    William Lane, an alleged British subject, in prison at Detroit, Mich., as well
                    as copy of a note which in consequence I addressed to Mr. Frelinghuysen,
                    requesting information as to the alleged statements made therein, and I have now
                    the honor to inclose copy of the reply thereto.</p>





